A||N||25||WhiteFieroBlur||Painting the back air vents||||1||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||06-01-2000||04:45 AM||||I was wondering, whats the best way to paint the 2 back air flow vents above the engine. Mine are very scratched and faded in color. Do I just clean them real good and just spray paint them with black spray paint or should I do a little something extra to make sure I do the job right and that it lasts? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||06-01-2000||05:02 AM||||Nothing special other than high-temp paint, so far as I know.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||06-01-2000||07:06 AM||||Im sure that you would need to put on many coats of clearcoat.||||reg||10
Z||000003||2M4 Dale||06-01-2000||07:40 AM||||I scuffed mine up with Scotchbrite first. Cleaned them really well. Then just painted them with high temp. satin black. I think they came out great !||||reg||1
Z||000004||wkayl||06-01-2000||09:05 AM||||I went to Auto Zone and bought a can of Dupli-Color trim paint.  I just washed the vents real good and painted them.  That was about 10 months ago and they still look new.||||reg||1
Z||000005||lennyb4||06-01-2000||09:32 AM||||I was actually thinking about having them chrome dipped  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> But i got to thinking about it and decided it sounded (and would probally look) alittle to ricey for me..||||reg||1
Z||000006||WhiteFieroBlur||06-01-2000||11:47 AM||||Chrome dipped? I hadn't though about that, I am not too sure how that would look. I have thought about getting my rims chrome dipped. I still have the stock rims on them and instead of getting new ones I thought about getting them chrome dipped. <P>  But thanx for the info on painting my vents I am gonna definatly do that in the next week or so. Cause I am sure it would make a huge difference. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||06-01-2000||12:11 PM||||Powder coat?||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||06-01-2000||12:35 PM||||DONT USE CLEARCOAT unless you want them glossy. besides I can guaranntee it will crack and peel very quickly. If you paint them I find that BBQ Grill black is great-right amount of gloss and hi-heat. Best by far would be powder coating, last forever. NOTE* dont ever get wax on them, youll never get it off and will have to paing them over again. Cant count how many Mustangs with flat black hoods ive hadto paint because someone waxed em.||||reg||1
Z||000009||contra||06-01-2000||01:21 PM||||i know you're all going to flame me for this probably, but i just steelwooled mine and washed em off, then flat black spray painted them up with about 3 coats throughout the day. they look perfect. i like the flat black look on them with all the little bumps.<BR>they look like they're plastic along with the rest of the car.<BR>just my 2 cents...i'm a cheapo so shoot me :)<BR>haha<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||86SE||06-01-2000||01:29 PM||||I used 400 grit sandpaper and black watercolor paint.  Thasts how cheap I am!||||reg||11
Z||000011||80's BOY||06-01-2000||01:32 PM||||if you know someone with a bead blaster, that would be an excellent prep. mine turned out great with clearcoat and all. are you tossing the honeycomb grille behind the vents?? i heard it is an air restictor but it keeps out leaves and snow. snow?? what is snow anyway?? i've never seen any!!||||reg||7
Z||000012||lennyb4||06-01-2000||01:37 PM||||You think thats cheap??? I took mine to the beach and rubbed them on the sand for a while then i colored them with my sons black crayons (that i got from denny's, didnt eat just used the bathroom)..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||Standard||06-01-2000||03:35 PM||||hehe. what a bunch of cheap punks!  <P>80's, I drilled that screen off of my GT vents awhile ago.  Leaves and stuff aren't that big of a problem, but the engine does seem to get a bit more dusty.||||reg||1
Z||000014||87ECO5||06-01-2000||03:40 PM||||Two hours before one of our Ohio Fiero cookouts, I decided to do mine.  I washed and rinsed them, dried them off and shot them with a few coats of Krylon satin black.<P>They turned out (and still look) perfect!||||reg||1
Z||000015||Alex4mula||06-01-2000||03:44 PM||||If you use BBQ paint test it before to see if you like the finish. I used one that came out flat black instead of the satin finish that I wanted. They look nice but was not exactly what I wanted. Will try again when they fade off, hope after couple of years.||||reg||1
